# Envelope limits for the conformance shakedown.
# Generated from ENVELOPE.md; run-agent.sh sources this file.
# 2026-07-12 calibration from the first real-CLI ticket (T-101), actual costs:
# - test-author (codex): $0.35
# - builder (claude) attempt 1: $0.69, hard-stopped by --max-budget-usd at the
#   old $0.50 per-run cap (context load alone exceeds it)
# - builder attempt 2: $1.48 (green, committed)
# Ticket cap raised mid-ticket ($4 -> $6.50) after the wrapper refused the
# reviewer run at $2.52 spent + $1.50 reserve — the refusal itself was correct
# behavior; the cap was mock-era. A real ticket ≈ $3-5 all-in.
# 2026-07-12 loop trial: daily cap 10 -> 13 — three tickets in one day
# (T-101 rows + T-102 + T-103) legitimately exceed 10; machine cap 15 still binds.
# Later same day: 13 -> 15 to match the machine cap — the repo cap tripping
# below the machine cap on a legitimate multi-ticket day adds an escalation
# without adding protection. The machine-level 15 is the hard stop.
# 2026-07-13 T-106 calibration: Claude test-author hit its hard stop at
# $1.57068 after producing the expected tests. Operator approved $2 per run and
# $10 per ticket so real 1M-context checking runs can finish without weakening
# the unchanged $15 repo and $20 machine daily caps.
PER_RUN_BUDGET_USD=2.00
PER_TICKET_BUDGET_USD=10.00
PER_RUN_MAX_TURNS=15
PER_RUN_TIMEOUT_MIN=5
DAILY_CAP_USD=15.00
